  "name": null,
  "problem": "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2{sin}^{2}⁡(3x+3y)-1.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡(g(x,y))=-6x+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant. What is $g(x,y)?$",
